-- CONTROL for #1075: byte-identical to main.mdk except the METHOD-LESS impl sits at a
-- DATA head (`Dog`) instead of the PRIMITIVE head `Int`.  That is the ONE flipped
-- dimension, and it is precisely the dimension main.mdk's abort keys on: a data head
-- owns constructors, so it carries a cell tag, so the arg-tag chain can test for it and
-- the receiver reaches the inherited default instead of falling off the end.
--
-- A green control proves the abort is about PRIMITIVE heads specifically and NOT about
-- method-less impls, generalized locals, cross-module defaults, or arg-tag dispatch in
-- general.  This program is also the exact shape #1046 was about; it build-runs to exit
-- 0 printing `woof|meow` since #1046's fix (sprint unmask-arg-tag-dispatch, S-1
-- `33385a53`), so this control doubles as that fix's standing regression guard now that
-- the #1046 must-fail row has drained and been deleted.
--
-- ⚠️ WHAT THE HARNESS ASSERTS HERE IS EXIT 0 AND NOTHING ELSE -- a control carries no
-- stdout pin.  Measured by hand: build exit 0, binary exit 0, stdout `woof|meow`.
import iface.{Speak(..), speak}

data Dog = Dog

data Cat = Cat

impl Speak Dog where              -- METHOD-LESS at a DATA head

impl Speak Cat where
  speak _ = "meow"

main =
  let f = v => speak v
  println (f Dog ++ "|" ++ f Cat)
